kwin 6.8: sample clients' wl_shm buffers in place on the memfd software device

Since 6.7 kwin wraps every client wl_shm buffer in a udmabuf and imports that into
the renderer, so client damage costs no texture upload. Without /dev/udmabuf that
fails, and on the memfd software device every damaged client region goes through
glTexSubImage2D into llvmpipe's texture memory first.

llvmpipe imports a dmabuf by mapping the whole fd and reading at the plane offset,
so the client's own pool memfd serves as that dmabuf just as kwin's render buffers
do in kwin-6.8-software-shm-presentation.patch. Hand it out as the buffer's
udmabuf attributes, with no device id, when rendering happens on the memfd device
and the pool carries F_SEAL_SHRINK (udmabuf demands the same seal, as a pool the
client shrinks would fault the renderer's threads). Only a software renderer's EGL
display imports such attributes; a GPU display, and every setup with udmabuf or a
render node, is unchanged. The dma-buf sync ioctls are skipped on a plain memfd.

Applies to kwin 6.8.x after kwin-6.8-software-shm-presentation.patch.

--- a/src/core/gpumanager.cpp
+++ b/src/core/gpumanager.cpp
@@ -367,6 +367,37 @@ std::optional<DmaBufAttributes> GpuManager::createUdmabuf(const ShmAttributes *a
 #endif
 }
 
+std::optional<DmaBufAttributes> GpuManager::createMemfdDmabuf(const ShmAttributes *attributes) const
+{
+    if (m_udmabuf.isValid() || !std::ranges::any_of(m_renderDevices, &RenderDevice::isMemfdDevice)) {
+        return std::nullopt;
+    }
+    // udmabuf refuses pools the client can shrink; the mapping would fault the same way here
+    const int seals = fcntl(attributes->fd.get(), F_GET_SEALS);
+    if (seals == -1 || !(seals & F_SEAL_SHRINK)) {
+        return std::nullopt;
+    }
+    struct stat buf;
+    if (fstat(attributes->fd.get(), &buf) == -1
+        || buf.st_size < attributes->offset + off_t(attributes->size.height()) * attributes->stride) {
+        return std::nullopt;
+    }
+    DmaBufAttributes ret;
+    ret.planeCount = 1;
+    ret.width = attributes->size.width();
+    ret.height = attributes->size.height();
+    ret.format = attributes->format;
+    ret.modifier = DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR;
+    ret.device = 0;
+    ret.fd[0] = attributes->fd.duplicate();
+    if (!ret.fd[0].isValid()) {
+        return std::nullopt;
+    }
+    ret.offset[0] = attributes->offset;
+    ret.pitch[0] = attributes->stride;
+    return ret;
+}
